Since I suggested killing the priest in this thread, even unaligned ...

On your way back up the priest does not have to be that tough.  (S)he
will not leave the altar even to save his/her life.  Digging wands are
plentiful so you can remove a wall and have a shooting gallery.  There
are more throwing rocks than you can carry in the mines, so have a line
of piles ready.  There are as many missile weapons as you can carry in
the mines as well.  Daggers, arrows, darts, etc.  Put them in a line of
piles to.  Start throwing and stay out of range.  The priest is toast
long before you run out of weapons most of the time but with an unlimited
supply of rocks that does not matter.  Take the hit in alignment, lost
telepathy, and convert the altar with something other than the priest's
body.  Then sacrafice enough to make up the lost alignment and enough to
max out your luck, pray enough to get back your telepathy.

This is very much a choice of tastes.  I take it as a quest to clear
the dungeon of nasty priests following those other guys.  Others chose
to not kill priests friendly or not.  Some value being able to purchase
protection more while I value early access to artifact weapons more.  I
also value maxed luck by the time I go below Sokoban, too.

If you've found another altar in the main mines by Sokoban, it's not
worth taking out the priest.  I tend to do a level of the main dungeon,
do a level of the mains, and cycle one level each until I've hit minetown
and Sokabon.  THen I do Sokoban, then the rest of the mines.  By the time
I come back up from minesend, I'm well prepared to take out a priest.

